I've had a similar configuration recently; found some +4 or +5 heavy
metal armor early on and didn't want to give up that enchantment. But
at some point when I found enough supporting armor (helmets, boots,
etc., maybe also some divine protection) to get AC below -5 (or so) I
switched to mithril, thereby giving up a few points of AC but gaining
speed as consequence of a better encumbrance level. Often the additional
speed helps more than a few points of AC; you can place more hits per
turn on average, you can flee from more monsters, and you can apply the
run/throw missiles tactics more often without getting in melee range
where the additional AC would be effective.

